AppGL — SPIRV-Cross MSL: report logical samplerBuffer size for 2D emulation

AppGL emulates non-native Metal texture buffers as a synthetic 2D texture.
For `textureSize(samplerBuffer)`, SPIRV-Cross previously emitted only
`texture.get_width()`, which returns the row width of the synthetic backing
texture rather than the logical texel count visible to GL shaders.

CTS `KHR-GL46.texture_buffer.texture_buffer_max_size` writes
`textureSize(sampler_buffer)` from a compute shader and expects
`GL_MAX_TEXTURE_BUFFER_SIZE`. With the AppGL buffer-texture row width at 8192,
the max-size backing is 8192 x 16384 texels, so logical size must be
`width * height`.

--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -11940,7 +11940,10 @@ void CompilerMSL::emit_instruction(const Instruction &instruction)
 		}
 
 		string expr = type_to_glsl(rslt_type) + "(";
-		expr += img_exp + ".get_width(" + lod + ")";
+		if (img_dim == DimBuffer && !msl_options.texture_buffer_native)
+			expr += img_exp + ".get_width() * " + img_exp + ".get_height()";
+		else
+			expr += img_exp + ".get_width(" + lod + ")";
 
 		// CKPT119 (AppGL): include DimRect (image2DRect / sampler2DRect) so
 		// imageSize / textureSize emit BOTH width and height. Upstream
